          <y:NodeLabel alignment="center" autoSizePolicy="content" fontFamily="Dialog" fontSize="12" fontStyle="plain" hasBackgroundColor="false" hasLineColor="false" height="253.919921875" horizontalTextPosition="center" iconTextGap="4" modelName="custom" textColor="#000000" verticalTextPosition="bottom" visible="true" width="938.06640625" x="2.9980468749998863" xml:space="preserve" y="36.4775390625">BERTopic Model Creation and Topic Discovery

After calculating the dynamic clustering parameters, the supporting models required for topic modeling are created and configured. These components include:

Sentence Transformer (MPNet) → Generates semantic embeddings (numerical vector representations) for each preprocessed document.
UMAP → Reduces the high-dimensional embedding vectors into a lower-dimensional space while preserving their semantic relationships, making clustering more efficient.
HDBSCAN → Groups semantically similar documents into clusters and automatically determines the number of topics while identifying outlier documents.
CountVectorizer → Creates a vocabulary of important words and n-grams from the clustered documents after removing stop words and filtering very common or very rare terms.
Class-TF-IDF (c-TF-IDF) → Calculates the importance of words within each cluster to identify the most representative keywords for every discovered topic.
Representation Models (Maximal Marginal Relevance, KeyBERTInspired, and Part-of-Speech Filtering) → Refine the 
topic representation by removing redundant keywords, selecting semantically meaningful terms, and retaining informative words such as nouns and adjectives.

After configuring these supporting components, a BERTopic model instance is created by passing them as
 parameters to the BERTopic() constructor. And after the prediction it will provide Topic and Probality of prediction is correct.
Topic have: Topic id, Name (topicId_topicname), respresentation_Docs(Full _text)
Important: Probablity is not consider any where....
Reduce Outlier:In this area topic -1 is considered to outlier we try to match those with any topic find using strategy="c-tf-idf", then also not matched with topic remains -1 
